m the roasting process because  it's very smoky these are really smoky  and very spicy  and they're very spicy and they do  release  a lot of  a lot of heat  [Music]  a little bit of salt green chili will  fall over the place what they do is they  actually put the green chili onto the  patty as it's cooking and then they  envelop  that green chili on the patty  with white american cheese  oh [ __ ]  oh yes  oh yeah  okay  you see this  wow  oh yeah that's perfect  there  oh the green chili cheeseburger  in my house  green chilies are hot obviously anytime  you eat spicy food it releases  endorphins when you're releasing  endorphins you feel kind of high so in a  way this burger kind of makes you high  it gives you a little buzz  [Laughter]  ah it's spicy that's very spicy the  smoked burger when you think about the  way a burger is normally cooked it's  usually cooked on a flat top something  that takes about five minutes smoking  usually takes a long time  hang on  whoa  oh [ __ ]  that come from  whoa  let's smoke a burger what i've done here  i've taken a classic backyard kettle  grill and i set it up for off set  smoking which basically means that i've  got coals on one side i'm going to put  the the burgers on the other side this  is going to sit here and smoke do you  want to know how long  50 minutes  the wood chips i use are mellow i don't  use hickory and mesquite you're much  better off using apple or elder woods  you don't want to overwhelm the flavor  of smoke  the key though is to make sure you keep  the smoke inside this thing 50 minutes  we're ready oh look at those oh yeah  i only put three things at a smoked  burger on a very uncomplicated squishy  roll  untoasted even first a slice of raw  onion in the bottom to protect the  bottom second put the patty  next i'm going to put the pickles on  dill pickle slices  and then  barbecue sauce any kind of barbecue  sauce  it's a smoked burger  smoke  that's ring good today i'm going to  teach you about a re